From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: ICompositor2 implicit animations and step easing

WinUI 2's NavigationView (Windows Terminal's settings page) gives its overflow button's visual an implicit Offset animation while it applies its template: it asks the compositor for ICompositor2 to make an ImplicitAnimationCollection and the visual for ICompositionObject2 to take it. Without them the template setup access-violated and the navigation menu was never filled. ICompositor2 makes implicit animation collections (a map of property names to animations, with its view and iterator) and step easing functions; the others it makes (lights, shadows, layer visuals, the newer brushes, animation groups) are not supported yet. A visual keeps its ImplicitAnimations, and setting a property the collection names runs that animation from the old value (this.StartingValue) to the new one (this.FinalValue). ICompositionAnimation2 keeps an animation's Target.
